# REQUIRES: verilator
# State rows in HBM behind a fixed on-chip scratch (foldsim-fold-static state-scratch-bits; the constant shell,
# cs_1109 INTERFACES.md section A). Whole classes stay resident while they fit in the scratch; a state-in-ram-pp
# class past it streams its rows from HBM. Its columns are a landing window of a fixed number of instance slots
# ({slot, row}, not {instance, row}). Each instance's P rows are prefetched into its slot at the state pass of the
# slot's previous occupant: virtual memories of {instance, row} rows, a chunk of columns each. Its passes read them in
# place as on chip and wait in a bubble while any row is pending. Each pass writes its row to HBM with its lanes as
# byte enables. Against the target, from zero state (Inputs/tb_pages.sv: a controller model per virtual memory),
# P = 2, 3 and 4 (Driver/Inputs/paged: a 160-bit register written on an enable, cut across rows), at response
# latencies of 1-60 host cycles, stalled channels, controllers out of room and bubbles, with the leaves' RAM virtual
# too. Folded pipelines (Driver/Inputs/fold_hbm) are tested with their stores in HBM as well. Small classes whose
# passes leave no room for a prefetch stay on chip. Under the default scratch, nothing streams, and the folded
# pipelines' stores take the scratch before HBM.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/paged
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/p2 --static --state-in-ram Leaf::2 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 Leaf > %t/p2.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=P2LOG < %t/p2.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=P2VH < %t/p2/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=P2DW < %t/p2/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/p2 -Mdir %t/p2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/p2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/p2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/p2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/p2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=1 +hi=60 +stall=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/p3 --static --state-in-ram Leaf::3 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 Leaf > %t/p3.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/p3 -Mdir %t/p3/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/p3/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/p3/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/p3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=5 +hi=60 +stall=20 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/p4b --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --bubbles --modulo Leaf > %t/p4b.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/p4b -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/p4b/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/p4b/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/p4b/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/p4b/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+6 +lo=5 +hi=40 +bubble=30 +full=10 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/ram --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --virtual-memories ram Leaf > %t/ram.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/ram -DVM1 -Mdir %t/ram/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/ram/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/ram/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/ram/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+9 +lo=1 +hi=40 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# Partly resident: a scratch of 2,000 bits holds two of the four instances' rows at P 8 (in RAMs of their own),
# the other two (every other state pass) stream through a window of one slot.
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/part --static --state-in-ram Leaf::8 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 2000 Leaf > %t/part.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PART < %t/part.log
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/part -Mdir %t/part/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/part/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/part/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/part/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/part/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=60 +stall=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# Copies of two instances each: no window fits (a prefetch between two passes P apart), so the rows stay on chip.
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/c2 --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --copies Leaf:2 Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=C2
# Default scratch: resident, as without it (no virtual memory).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/on --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ON
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONVH < %t/on/foldsim_sim.vh
# Folded pipelines, their stores in HBM too (three virtual memories), and with bubbles.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/fold_hbm
